### Health Check and Utility Endpoints

### Import variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4001
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Health Check - Basic
# @name healthCheck
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Health Check - Verify Response Structure
# @name healthCheckDetailed
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### Expected Response:
# {
#   "status": "healthy",
#   "timestamp": "2025-07-03T10:00:00Z",
#   "version": "1.0.0"
# }

###

### 3. Health Check - Server Load Test
# @name healthCheckLoadTest
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Metrics Endpoint (if available)
# @name metrics
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. Health Check - Invalid Method
# @name healthCheckInvalidMethod
POST {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{}

###

### 6. Health Check - With Query Parameters (should be ignored)
# @name healthCheckWithParams
GET {{baseUrl}}/health?test=value&invalid=param
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Health Check - Different Accept Headers
# @name healthCheckTextPlain
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: text/plain

###

### 8. Health Check - No Accept Header
# @name healthCheckNoAccept
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

###

### 9. Root Endpoint Test (if available)
# @name rootEndpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. Non-Existent Utility Endpoint
# @name nonExistentUtility
GET {{baseUrl}}/status
Accept: application/json

###
